  <p>
    <strong>The GarageCloud workshop board is a live view of every bay and every job, updated in real time.</strong>
    It replaces the whiteboard or the wall of job cards with the same at-a-glance layout, minus the bit where
    someone has to physically update it and everyone else has to walk over to read it.
  </p>

  <h2>What's on the board</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every bay, with the vehicle and job currently in it.</li>
    <li>Job status — waiting, in progress, ready — visible without opening the job card.</li>
    <li>Registration, job type and technician assigned, at a glance.</li>
    <li>Mobile and courtesy car jobs alongside in-bay work, on the same board.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why a live board beats a whiteboard</h2>
  <p>
    A physical whiteboard works for one workshop location and however many people can see it. It breaks down the
    moment a technician is on a mobile job, a manager wants status from home, or two people update the same card at
    once. A live board is the same information, visible to whoever needs it, from wherever they are.
  </p>

  <h2>How job cards move through the board</h2>
  <p>
    Each job starts when it is booked, gets assigned a bay and a technician, and moves through status as work
    progresses — from waiting, through in progress, to ready for collection or delivery. Reassigning a bay or
    technician is a change on the board itself, not a rewrite of a paper card.
  </p>
